<p>Everything below was recorded by a data file at the moment this page was built:</p>
<dl class="data-files-demo">
  <div class="data-files-demo__row">
    <dt>Built</dt>
    <dd><time datetime="{{ build.builtAt }}">{{ build.builtAt | readableDateTime }}</time><span data-time-ago="{{ build.builtAt | htmlDateString }}" data-time-ago-prefix=" · " hidden></span></dd>
  </div>
  <div class="data-files-demo__row">
    <dt>Triggered by</dt>
    <dd>
      {%- if build.hookTitle %}the “{{ build.hookTitle }}” build hook
      {%- elif build.context == "local" %}a build on someone's own machine
      {%- else %}a git push or a manual deploy{% endif -%}
    </dd>
  </div>
  <div class="data-files-demo__row">
    <dt>Netlify context</dt>
    <dd>{{ build.context }}</dd>
  </div>
  <div class="data-files-demo__row">
    <dt>Commit</dt>
    <dd>{% if build.commit %}<a href="{{ site.repoUrl }}/commit/{{ build.commit }}"><code>{{ build.commit }}</code></a>{% else %}not available outside Netlify{% endif %}</dd>
  </div>
</dl>
<p>On the live site, a scheduled rebuild shows up here as the build hook, with the same commit as the day before: nothing in the repo changed, but the build-time data did.</p>
